  "worked_solution": "To find the roots of $f(x),$ we must solve $f(x)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\sqrt[6]{24x+13}-1=0\n$$\n\nWe solve this equation by making $x$ the subject, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{24x+13}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{24x+13} & =1 \\\\ {(\\sqrt[6]{24x+13})}^{6} & ={1}^{6} \\\\ 24x+13 & =1 \\\\ 24x & =-12 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we must check the answer by substituting it back into the initial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[6]{24\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})+13}-1 & =0 \\\\ \\sqrt[6]{1}-1 & =0 \\\\ 0 & =0\\,\u2713\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the root of $f(x)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$",
